{
  "_comment": [
    "ENGINE CONTRACT — captured from the real loci engine, not hand-authored.",
    "Regenerate READS with:   ./capture-fixtures.sh <vault> --write-contract",
    "Regenerate EFFECTS with: ./capture-effects.py --write-contract",
    "",
    "Two capture routes because the two halves have different ground truth. For a",
    "READ the CLI envelope is the wire envelope, so the CLI is honest. For an EFFECT",
    "it is not: the CLI projects a CommandPreview ({command, changes, refusals,",
    "_committed}) while the LSP host sends the SourceCommit ({document, commit,",
    "revision}). Project 004 captured effects from the CLI and validated the fake",
    "against a shape the client never sees — two live bugs (F-14, F-15) and one",
    "invented enum value (F-16) came out of that blind spot. capture-effects.py",
    "speaks JSON-RPC to a real loci-lsp instead.",
    "",
    "fs_v2.py validates its DEFAULTS against this file at startup and refuses to",
    "run on drift. This is what enforces the 004 R6 rule (a fixture must share the",
    "engine's shape, width, and vocabulary) by CONSTRUCTION rather than by",
    "discipline -- the original statusline bug shipped because the rule was only a",
    "convention and nothing checked it.",
    "",
    "It records the engine's CONTRACT (key sets, row arities, enums, widths), not",
    "captured rows: the suite asserts on known fixture paths like 'notes/a.md', so",
    "pasting real vault data wholesale would break every test while proving less."
  ],
